+# Corpus fetching: rate limits and mirrors
+
+Source: `manifest.tsv` header (files located via GitHub code search on
+2026-09-12, fetched raw via `raw.githubusercontent.com`) plus this project's
+own fetch-session transcripts (Svipall fetch tool), which recorded the
+concrete limit values and the mirror fallback chain below.
+
+## Per-domain rate limit
+
+- **12 visits per 60 s window**, per domain.
+- Breaching the limit triggers a **900 s (15 min) cooldown** before that
+  domain is fetched from again.
+
+## Hosts used
+
+Fetches were attempted against these hosts, in order, falling back on
+failure/exhaustion:
+
+1. `raw.githubusercontent.com` — primary source, confirmed by
+   `manifest.tsv`'s own header comment.
+2. `cdn.jsdelivr.net` (as `cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/<owner>/<repo>@<branch>/<path>`) — mirror fallback.
+3. `cdn.statically.io` — secondary mirror fallback; observed to be slow and
+   prone to timeouts.
+
+`GATE1.md` notes the corpus was fetched incrementally because of this rate
+limiting (115 of 323 manifest entries were on disk at measurement time).
+
+## Provenance note
+
+The rate-limit numbers and the mirror list beyond `raw.githubusercontent.com`
+are not recorded anywhere in this repository's tracked files (manifest.tsv,
+GATE1.md, etc.) — they come from this project's own fetch-session transcript
+history. If you need to re-verify them independently of that history, re-run
+the fetch and observe the tool's own throttling/cooldown behavior.
